Hash: SHA512

annotations:
  artifacthub.io/changes: |-
    - kind: changed
      description: "Updated the edge image to v4.10.0, which no longer has to trust a client-sent X-Forwarded-For and can read PROXY protocol headers. Fair-share admission and the access log now see the real client IP behind ingress controllers and cloud load balancers; previously a client could get a fresh fair-share bucket per request, or every client shared one."
    - kind: added
      description: "clientIP.mode (default auto) configures client-IP handling for your provider: PROXY protocol on AWS, DigitalOcean and Linode LoadBalancers (the chart adds the provider's annotation to the edge Service), externalTrafficPolicy Local on GKE and Azure LoadBalancers, and trusted X-Forwarded-For hops behind an Ingress. No CIDRs needed; clientIP.trustedProxies is optional."
    - kind: added
      description: "New edge metric imageengine_edge_client_ip_resolutions_total shows how each client IP was chosen, and an install note warns when an Ingress and a LoadBalancer Service both expose the edge."
  artifacthub.io/signKey: |
    fingerprint: C3A55111ED91FEDE4A82A4B4463266060957C4B3
